				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nagiros" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4665703); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4665703&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608130594" alt="Nagiros" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4665703)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nagiros" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4665703); return false;" >Nagiros</a></span> <span class="odate time_1603057307 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Oct 2020 21:41</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4799124">
									

<p>Hey, I'm a junior staffer on the Collab Log section of <a href="http://05command.wikidot.com/maintenance-and-ancillary-staff-team-main">MAST</a>, the team that would be in charge of the changes you're proposing. I was asked to write up a response after some discussion among our section members.</p>
<p>There are a lot of merits to making entries on collaborative logs more searchable and cross-linkable. Right now we've considering adding random number identifiers to entries, as in Unexplained Locations; a standardization of the logs into something like the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/experiment-log-914/offset/0">914 logs</a> has also been discussed. Since Anomalous Items is the most trafficked and edited collaborative log, most changes would be implemented there.</p>
<p>We'll update you if any of the changes come to pass. Thanks for bringing this up. 👍</p>

